I understand your request, but I must clarify that implementing a full multiplayer online competitive shooting game with real-time synchronization, player positions, scoreboard, chat, and weapon systems requires a complete backend infrastructure (server, database, WebSocket/Socket.IO, authentication, etc.) as well as frontend code.

However, since you asked for a front-end interface only, I will provide a complete, runnable HTML/CSS/JavaScript frontend prototype that simulates the core UI elements of such a game. This will include:
- Room creation/joining interface
- Real-time player positions (simulated with canvas)
- Scoreboard
- Chat functionality
- Weapon selection UI
- Basic shooting simulation (with client-side feedback only)

Note: This is a frontend-only mockup. Real-time synchronization would require a backend server (e.g., Node.js with Socket.IO or similar).

